*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !SELIDXV(index, value, has.value, file, list)
*
* SELECTINDEX into a select list variable.  The SELECTINDEX goes to numbered list 10 and !MOVELIST (MOVELISTV) moves that
* list into LIST, which leaves list 10 empty: list 10 is this statement's scratch list, and what it held is lost.  With
* HAS.VALUE the ids of the records that have VALUE are selected, otherwise the indexed values.  An index the file does not
* have leaves STATUS() at 1, as SELECTINDEX does, and LIST holds an empty list.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

subroutine selidxv(index, value, has.value, file, list)
$catalog !selidxv

   if has.value then
      selectindex index, value from file to 10
   end else
      selectindex index from file to 10
   end
   if status() then
      * an index the file does not have: an empty list, and nothing run after the SELECTINDEX that could change STATUS()
      list = ''
      return
   end
   call !movelist(10, list, 0, 1)
   return
end

* END-CODE
